# shir_nodes/field_strip.node — expression-level semantic IR node.
# The cursor advance behind `${s#*D}`: the ABSOLUTE byte offset just past
# the first `delim` at/after `off` — or `off` UNCHANGED when no `delim`
# follows it (bash's strip is a no-op when the pattern does not match,
# so the cursor must not move). The result is a decimal STRING (the same
# channel every shell scalar number travels), consumed by the companion
# FieldGrab reads of the same cursor var. Emitted by `str-chop-cursor`.
#
# Backends: C (memchr-free strchr-at-offset; target-gated offer).
# Fallback: sh2.fieldStrip(text, off, delim)

node FieldStrip
tag "FieldStrip"
kind expr
field text: expr
field off: expr
field delim: string
spec: none (unstated)
